#   3773:  18706: ! 
#   3773:  18707: ! {******************************************************************************
#   3773:  18708: ! 
#   3773:  18709: ! Output real "economy" format
#   3773:  18710: ! 
#   3773:  18711: ! Outputs a real in minium space, preferably without an exponent. The economy
#   3773:  18712: ! format is designed both to take minimum space, but still give the maximum
#   3773:  18713: ! number of significant digits, and to remove the exponent if possible, by
#   3773:  18714: ! placing it within the number.
#   3773:  18715: ! 
#   3773:  18716: ! To do this, the number is converted, in ascii, to the floating point buffer
#   3773:  18717: ! in a large buffer. Then, the exponent is read from the number, and blanked
#   3773:  18718: ! out. The decial point is removed, and the number normalized to decimal point
#   3773:  18719: ! left. If the decimal point can be placed within the number, it is. Also, we
#   3773:  18720: ! allow a certain number of zeros before and after the number, as long as they
#   3773:  18721: ! don't exceed the size of an exponent in ASCII. If the decimal still cannot be
#   3773:  18722: ! placed, then the number reverts to floating point format, abet with the
#   3773:  18723: ! trailing zeros removed.
#   3773:  18724: ! 
#   3773:  18725: ! ******************************************************************************}
